  "notes": "USAGE: {連続|れんぞく} emphasizes the unbroken sequence of events or things happening in succession.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・〜{連続|れんぞく}で (for ~ in a row, ~ consecutive)\n・{連続|れんぞく}する (to continue, to occur consecutively)\n・{連続|れんぞく}ドラマ (TV series, serial drama)\n・{連続|れんぞく}{殺人|さつじん} (serial killings)\n\nCONTRAST:\n・{連続|れんぞく} - emphasizes consecutive occurrence\n・{継続|けいぞく} - emphasizes ongoing continuation of an action",
